# Plan style

A plan must read as if it was just written. State only the current design.

- No references to earlier drafts: "previously", "in the last plan", "as discussed above", "changed from", "instead of X".
- No change logs, revision notes, or "updated:" markers inside the plan.
- When the user revises a plan, rewrite the affected sections in place so the result reads as one coherent first version.

**Avoid:**

```text
Earlier we had subdirs per repo; now the layout is flat.
Renamed `work/` to `nb_runs/` (see previous plan).
```

**Prefer:**

```text
Notebooks are staged flat in `$SCRATCHDIR/notebooks/`; run data goes to `$SCRATCHDIR/nb_runs/<stem>/`.
```
